{{/*
  on-call/shared/playbook-files — the canonical, folder-remembered file
  parameters for the investigation and escalation playbooks, shared by every
  On-Call prompt that inlines a runbook. Extracted so the parameter names,
  defaults, and folder-scoped `remember` semantics stay identical across
  "On-Call: I have been paged" and "On-Call: watch and investigate" — a path
  picked in one carries into the other because both key the remembered value on
  the same parameter name.

  This fragment defines NO body text; it only documents the shared parameter
  contract for maintainers. The parameters themselves live in each prompt's
  `parameters:` block (YAML front-matter cannot be templated), but they MUST be
  copied verbatim from the contract below so the two prompts stay in sync:

      parameters:
        - name: InvestigationInstructions
          type: filename
          required: false
          default: .mitto/cso/investigation.md
          dir: .mitto/cso
          glob:
            - "*.md"
          remember: folder
          description: >-
            Workspace-relative primary investigation playbook, inlined verbatim
            into every child investigator's prompt. Defaults to
            `.mitto/cso/investigation.md`.
        - name: EscalationInstructions
          type: filename
          required: false
          default: .mitto/cso/escalation.md
          dir: .mitto/cso
          glob:
            - "*.md"
          remember: folder
          description: >-
            Workspace-relative escalation playbook, consulted when a credible
            mitigation cannot be found. Defaults to `.mitto/cso/escalation.md`.

  Callers resolve the effective paths at the top of their body with:

      {{ $investigationFile := Arg "InvestigationInstructions" ".mitto/cso/investigation.md" }}
      {{ $escalationFile := Arg "EscalationInstructions" ".mitto/cso/escalation.md" }}
*/ -}}
